            <ArticleTitle>Development of κ Opioid Receptor Agonists by Focusing on Phenyl Substituents of 4-Dimethylamino-3-phenylpiperidine Derivatives: Structure-Activity Relationship Study of Matrine Type Alkaloids.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>420-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1248/cpb.c15-00963</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of new κ opioid receptor (KOR) agonists were developed from the lead compound 4-dimethylamino-1-pentanoylpiperidine (3), a matrine-type alkaloid. Derivatives of 3 were synthesized with a variety of phenyl substituents and evaluated for their antinociceptive effects. Additionally, their selectivity for an opioid receptor was investigated for cis-4c and d, and trans-4g, all of which had high activity exerted through the KOR.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
